  "lore": {
    "energy": "A shielded continuous-power core charges a 1.2 GJ pulse store between passes; solar wings run the bus, cryocoolers and optical control.",
    "thermal": "Phase-change heat sinks absorb a burn, then the paired radiator vanes unfold and reject heat before the next firing opportunity.",
    "optics": "A two-axis ventral telescope steers a continuous 1.064 µm beam. The engine drives OPTICS_YAW and OPTICS_PITCH and creates all beam and ground effects.",
    "name": "The owner named SOL-82 as an homage to SOL-740 and 1982."
  },
